0 103 560 [
[(This patch attempts to scrub the noise floor from a sample in two)]
[(steps. First using the "make-mask" message \050which is caught in the)]
[([pd fft-analysis] subpatch\051, you estimate the background spectrum.)]
[(You would normally do this at a moment when only the background)]
[(noise is audible. Then, turn on "masking" \050to 15 by default, but try)]
[(other values\051 and the patch will try to clean the background noise)]
[(out of a signal.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 103 454 [
[(For this demonstration, you control the amplitudes of a looping)]
[(sample and a filtered noise source. Normally you'd hit "calculate)]
[(noise mask" with only the noise turned on, then turn both the noise)]
[(and the sampler on, and also "masking", to see if the patch can)]
[(clean the noise out of the signal. Open the [pd fft-analysis] window)]
[(to see the algorithm, or the "insample" window to change samples, or)]
[("mask-table" to see the current mask \050the average signal power of)]
[(the noise to clean out of the signal\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
